1 NAME Maria /Gattilusio/
2 GIVN Maria
2 SURN Gattilusio
2 _MARNM Kommenos-Hatun
1 SEX F
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20LORDSHIPS%20IN%20GREECE.htm#MariaGattilusainaMAlexanderTrebizond
2 CONT
2 CONT (f)        MARIA Gattilusaina.  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names Maria Gattilusio as the wife of Alexander, son of Emperor Alexios[717].  Laonicus Chalcocondylas records that "rex Alexius…filium suum…Scantarim" married "fili
2 CONC am Galiuzis…Mitylenis" during the lifetime of his father[718].  Pero Tafur, Spanish ambassador, records a meeting with Alexander in Constantinople in Nov 1437 and a subsequent visit to Trebizond, the description indicating that Al
2 CONC exander´s marriage had taken place shortly before[719].  Runciman states that she was taken prisoner by the Ottomans after they entered the city of Trebizond 15 Aug 1461, and entered the harem of Sultan Mohammed II[720].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (1437) ALEXANDER [Skantarios] Megas Komnenos co-Emperor in Trebizond, son of ALEXIOS IV Emperor in Trebizond & his wife Theodora Kantakuzene (-[1454/59][721]). 
