1 OCCU Countess of Maldeghem, gravin van Lalaing! dame du Palais de la Reine des Pays-Bas, Femme de Lettres
1 TITL Comtessa
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''THE GERMAN BRANCH OF THE MALDEGHEM FAMILY'''
2 CONT
2 CONT To make the descent and family of Marie Henriette van Maldeghem a bit clearer, let's follow a family tree of mainly the German branch below. Let's go back in time for a moment: Jean Dominique van Maldeghem (1662-1747) enters into 
2 CONC a second marriage on 31 November 1715 with Anna Amour Florence van Haudion. The couple has six children, including Charles Florent Joseph, with whom the German connection begins.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''I. Charles Florent Joseph van Maldeghem''' (10 July 1722 - +1 November 1783)
2 CONT Married on December 19, 1750 to Maria Philippine van Stain, daughter of Karl Leopold van Stain, heiress of Niederstotzingen.
2 CONT Karl Leopold of Stain (Brussels, December 24, 1729 - +Niederstotzingen, March 5, 1809) married Countess Charlotte Philippine d'Ursel in 1773. The couple lived alternately in Brussels and Niederstotzingen. Already since 1457, Niede
2 CONC rstotzingen has been owned by the family of Stain and for 350 years they left their mark on the town. At the end of the 18th century, Karl Leopold inherited Niederstotzingen and the surrounding villages. In 1778, he had the old, d
2 CONC ilapidated castle torn down and a new one built in the style of the time, with French influence. He holds several high offices at the court of Empress Maria Theresa and of Emperor Joseph Il, and he is also a member of high knighth
2 CONC oods. In 1779, Joseph Il elevated him to the peerage and allowed him the title of count. Joseph Franz Maximilian, his only son (01 April 7, 1776), dies at an early age.
2 CONT Heirs to the countship of Niederstotzingen, Riedhausen and Bergenweiler become: Joseph Alexander François of Maldeghem, son of his late sister Maria Philippine, and a sister of Count Karl Leopold who resides as a stiftsdame in the
2 CONC  monastery of Dale in the Jura.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ll. JOSEPH ALEXANDER FRANÇOIS VAN MALDEGHEM''' (July 11, 1754 - +Brussels, October 17, 1809), son of Charles Florent and Maria Philippine van Stain, count of Maldeghem and of Steenhuffel, baron of Leischoot, lord of Haybes, cap
2 CONC tain of the grenadiers in the regiment of the prince de Ligne, chief hunting master of Brabant, marries Marie
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000187444042821&size=large}}, {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000187443942833&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Ghislaine d'Argenteau (0Morawetz/Mähren, Feb. 28, 1764 - + March 25, 1801). Count Joseph Alexander François, heir to Charles Florent Joseph, dies before the inheritance is settled. This passes to his son Karl Leopold Ludwig (
2 CONC see below). After the death in 1817 of the stifts lady in Dale, her property also passes to Count Karl Leopold Ludwig.
2 CONT From the marriage of Count Joseph Alexander François to Countess Marie Anne three children are born:
2 CONT
2 CONT …1. Marie Louise Madeleine Joseph Ghislaine (December 01, 1785) who married Georges, Marquis de Trazegnies on May 13, 1804 and had two children!
2 CONT A. Alexander Gillion de Trazegnies
2 CONT B. Nathalie de Trazegnies (07 September 1811 - +4 June 1835) who married Eugène de Ligne on 21 July 1835
2 CONT
2 CONT …2. Marie Henriette Octavie Ghislaine (12 August 1787 - +12 August 1866)
2 CONT Married May 11, 1807, to Charles de Lalaing (October 28, 1768 - +August 24, 1816). The Maldeghem la Loyale writer had two children:
2 CONT A. Maximilien de Lalaing (Brussels, April 24, 1811 - +Brussels, December 12, 1881) who marries Julie Ann Vibart (Ramport Boleah, Bengal, 6 janu ari 1830 - +Brussels, February 27, 1912) in London on April 17, 1855. They had six chi
2 CONC ldren:
2 CONT a. Charles Maximilien (0SaintJohn de Paddington, March 4, 1857 - +Uccle,December 12, 1919) who married Baroness Christine du Tour de Bellinchove.
2 CONT b. Jacques Henry Eduard (0London, November 4, 1858 - +Brussels, October 10, 1917), painter and sculptor, member of the Royal Academy and of the Commission on Monuments and Sites, etc.
2 CONT c. Maria Jeanne (Brussels, December 24, 1856 - +Brussels April 7, 1927).
2 CONT d. Antoine Maximilien (0Brussels, October 1, 1866 - +Trondheim, June 25, 1916).
2 CONT e. Philippe Harold (twin brother of previous, Brussels, +15 March 1916).
2 CONT f. Maximilien Enguerrand Simon (Boulogne-sur-mer, August 4, 1869 - +Oostkamp, July 28, 1943) married Madeleine Peers de Nieuwburgh on November 28, 1901.
2 CONT B. Camille Ange de Lalaing (0Brussels, April 23, 1813 - +Brussels, September 19, 1840) marries Baron Auguste Charles d'Overschie (July 27, 1806) on July 20, 1836. From that marriage, Arthur Henri d'Overschie was born on July 12, 1
2 CONC 837. After the death of Camille Ange, Auguste d'Overschie enters a second marriage in 1851 to the German countess Stéphanie Clémentine Caroline van Nesselrode d'Ereshoven
2 CONT (December 06, 1818 - died suddenly on June 10, 1881 in Kreuznach).
2 CONT Three children were born to this marriage:
2 CONT …a. Valentine Caroline Emmanuelle (May 15, 1856) 
2 CONT …b. Léon Auguste Alexandre (May 19, 1857)
2 CONT …c. Isabelle Joséphine (August 4, 1859)
2 CONT
2 CONT …3. Charles Leopold Louis (follows under III and bears a German name)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''III. KARL LEOPOLD LUDWIG VON MALDEGHEM''' (Münster, in exile, on April 18, 1797 - +lgling, July 27, 1877) married Maria Theresia Ludowica von Waldburg-Zeil-Wurzach (Wurzach, Aug. 26, 1800 - +Cannstatt, Oct. 13, 1856) on June 24
2 CONC , 1823 in Wurzach.
2 CONT Karl Leopold was taken as a hostage to Paris at the age of seven, during the Napoleonic Wars, by order of Emperor Napoleon 1, where he was trained for a military career in the strict mi litary academy of Saint-Cyr. From 1811 to 18
2 CONC 14, he is page to the emperor. Later he becomes chamberlain of the Dutch king, honorary knight of the Order of Malta, bearer of the Commander's Cross of the French Legion of Honor and hereditary Reichsrat of the Bavarian crown.
2 CONT It is Karl Leopold who comes into possession of the noble property of the fa milie von Stain in 1809. The count settles permanently in Niederstotzingen and sells all his possessions in Belgium, France and Bohemia. With the proceed
2 CONC s he buys, for 226,000 guilders, the castle and estate of Oberstotzingen, Kaltenburg, Reuendorf and the knight's estate of Stetten. In 1830, he is able to repurchase several borrows, forests and lands, which had been sold to the K
2 CONC aisheim monastery in 1661 and had come into the possession of the Würtemberg crown in 1802, for the sum of 133,000 guilders. As a result, the old von Stain property once again formed one large whole,
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000187443751843&size=large}}
2 CONT Graaf Karl Leopold Ludwig von Maldeghem ( 1797- 1877), broer van Madame de Lalaing.
2 CONT
2 CONT consisting of: Niederstotzingen, Bergenweiler, Stetten, Kaltenburg and Oberstotzingen. In Niederstotzingen he further owned the Freihaus, the tithe barn, farms and guest houses. In the fens owned by the count, the population of Ni
2 CONC ederstotzingen burned peat for a long time; it was the only fuel.
2 CONT Only in the first half of the 19th century did feudalism come to an end in Germany: taxes and feudal services were abolished, land was allocated to the peasants, customary law disappeared and in 1806 the gallows - an odious symbol
2 CONC  of medieval justice - was dismantled in Niederstotzingen. From 1811, Niederstotzingen becomes an independent municipality, governed by a bailiff and an elected town council. Outwardly, the power of the count disappeared.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000187443976821&size=large}}
2 CONT Gravin Maria Theresia Ludowica von Waldburg-Zeil-Wurzach (1800-1856), echtgenote van graaf Karl Leopold Ludwig von Maldeghem.
2 CONT
2 CONT The castle was expanded by a pair of wings in 1821. To the castle belonged a renter's house and a gatehouse - now converted into the Schloss-Passage, luxurious apartments - which housed the offices of the count, of the administrat
2 CONC or of the domains, of the forester, etc. Here the administration of the forests, the accounting of the brewery, the collection of rents from possessions in Hasslankreuth, lgling, Riedhausen, Reuendorf , of the guest courts, lands,
2 CONC  houses and farms in Niederstotzingen, Obertotzingen, Stetten, Hürben, Burgberg and Bergenweiler took place. Yellow-red painted windows of a house, farm or gasthof were the sign of ownership of the Count von Maldeghem. The castle 
2 CONC also had a flower and vegetable garden and greenhouse to provide the castle with fresh flowers at all times,
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000187443320888&size=large}}
2 CONT Schloss N iederstotzingen, in 1778 gebouwd door Carl Leopold van Stain in 1821 uitgebreid door Karl
2 CONT Leopold Ludwig van Maldeghem.
2 CONT
2 CONT and fresh vegetables. Vegetables were also sold and the gärtnerei was believed after World War I for its modern management. In 1956, both flower and vegetable cultivation disappeared.
2 CONT The present Peter and Paul Church in Niederstotzingen was completely demolished and rebuilt in 1844 thanks to a generous gift from Count Karl Leopold, who provided 36,500 of the 50,000 guilders. It remained a "simultaneous church"
2 CONC  for some time, as it was used by both Catholics and Protestants. The church stands on the grounds of the castle. In 1836, Count Karl also had a presbytery built behind the church, next to his castle park.
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Leopold and Maria Theresa had thirteen children, several of whom died at birth or shortly thereafter:
2 CONT 1 . Georg Guillaume Maria (Niederstotzingen, April 18, 1822 - +Algiers, July 5, 1845, buried in Niederstotzingen). He was a lieutenant in the royal Würtemberg guard.
2 CONT 2. Oscar (Niederstotzingen, 16 May 1825, died the same day) and Charles (two ling brother, + 18 May 1825 at 4 p.m., both buried in Niederstotzingen).
2 CONT 3. Edmund Leopold Maria (Niederstotzingen, 16 July 1826 - +Niederstotzingen, 15 August 1826).
2 CONT 4. '''Ottmar''' Carl Maria (Niederstotzingen, October 30, 1827 - +Friedrichshafen, March 4, 1860, buried in Niederstotzingen) married Thérèse Fugger zu Glött, Oberndorf und Hilgartsberg (July 28, 1829 - +December 8, 1899) on Novem
2 CONC ber 17, 1857. Thérèse is a daughter of Sebastian and a granddaughter of Reichsgrave Leopold Fugger zu Glött, Königliches Bayerisches Regierungspräsident. Count Ottmar is chamberlain at the court of Würtemberg. Shortly after the de
2 CONC ath of the count, a son of his also dies, on
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000187443843821&size=large}}
2 CONT Schloss Oberstotzingen, eertijds eigendom van de familie von Maldeghem, nu omgebouwd tot een luxueus hotel.
2 CONT
2 CONT after all, on his grave plate we read: "lhm folgte bald ins Grab sein Sohn". This son is Arnuld (December 20, 1859 - April 7, 1860). Another son, Edmond (18 November 1858 - +6 June 1912) married Elisabeth Weichert. It is to her co
2 CONC usin Ottmar that Madame de Lalaing dedicates her book Maldeghem la Loyale. 
2 CONT 5. Karl Joseph Maria (follows under IV) 
2 CONT 6. Edmond (Niederstotzingen, 28 May 1831 - +Graz, 10 September 1909) married Française Schwartz on 24 July 1880. 
2 CONT 7. Camill (Niederstotzingen, December 17, 1832 - +Gainfarn, May 10, 1900), royal eunuch, lieutenant and knight of the Sovereign Maltese Order. 
2 CONT 8. Arthur (Niederstotzingen, July 21, 1835 - +Pressbourg, May 21, 1912) marries on June 6 1868 with Georgine Maria Thérèse Bauer (August 15, 1848 - +Meran, April 30, 1907). 
2 CONT 9. Maximilian (Niederstotzingen, July 29, 1836 - + August 13, 1836). 
2 CONT 10. Max Friedrich Maria (Niederstotzingen, August 17, 1837 - August 29, 1837) 
2 CONT 11. Heinrich Karl Maria (Niederstotzingen, February 19, 1840 - May 20, 1876), royal chamberlain, first lieutenant, holder of the War Medal. 
2 CONT 12. Arnuld Leopold Maria (Niederstotzingen, 2 May 1841 - +2 February 1842). 
2 CONT
2 CONT On the grave slab of Countess Maria Theresia, in the funerary chapel in the cemetery of Niederstotzingen, her whole life is depicted in a few striking lines:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gattenliebe, Mutterliebe
2 CONT Trug Sie in sich Treu und warm 
2 CONT Wolhltun war /hr ganzes Wesen 
2 CONT Licht vom bangen Traum genesen 
2 CONT Ruht Sie in Marias Arm.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000187443552832&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT '''IV. KARL JOSEPH MARIA''' (Niederstotzingen, 11 January 1829 - +Niederstotzingen, 12 February 1913) hereditary Reichsrat of the Bavarian Crown, Captain, Grand Commander at the Royal Court of Bavaria, Knight of the Order of St. G
2 CONC regory, marries 27 November 1861 in Vienna in the Schottenkirche with Countess Maria Cajetana Franzisca Andràssy van Csik-Szent-Király und Kraszna-Horka (Hosssureth, Hungary, November 30, 1834 - +Munich, October 18, 1916). Countes
2 CONC s Maria Cajetana was 'Sternkreuzordensdame', she founded a hospital in Niederstotzingen, for which she donated 4000 guilders. The count acquires a lot of property in the center of Niederstotzingen, for example in 1906 he bought th
2 CONC e hotel Krone near his castle for 227,000 marks. That he was very popular with the population is shown by the celebration in 1909 of his eightieth birthday. Almost the entire population took part in a torchlight procession that le
2 CONC d to the castle under musical accompaniment. There the mayor congratulated the count on behalf of the entire municipality and at the end of his speech everyone shouted: "Hoch, hoch, hoch!" The count thanked everyone, after which t
2 CONC he procession went through the park to the market place. who bought beer from the Stettener Schloss brewery - and almost all of them did! - poured Freibier all evening. Karl Joseph Maria and Maria Cajetana lived in Niederstotzinge
2 CONC n Castle, where following children were born:
2 CONT 1 . Eugen Maria (Niederstotzingen, 12 December 1862 - +30 December 1862). 
2 CONT 2. Ludwig Karl Maria (follows under V) 
2 CONT 3. Arnold Paul Maria (Niederstotzingen, 20 July 1865 - + 15 January 1937), last commander of the 2 Garden-Ulanenregiments, holder of several decorations "undander hoher Orden". 
2 CONT 4. Georg Peter Maria (Niederstotzingen, 7 June 1867 - +28 February 1969).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''V. LUDWIG KARL MARIA VON MALDEGHEM''' (Niederstotzingen, 25 July 1864 - +7 November 1936) Hereditary Reichsrat of the Bavarian Crown, Grand Commander of the Royal Court of Bavaria, Knight of the Order of Saint Gregory, married 
2 CONC 25 August 1902 in Pressburg (Hungary) Countess Maria Bianca Dezasse de Petit-Verneuille (Görz, April 4, 1875 - +Ulm, August 25, 1945).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ludwig Karl Maria and Maria Bianca have the following children: 
2 CONT 1 . Franz Karl Anton Maria (0lgling, June 26, 1903 - +July 2, 1923). 
2 CONT 2. Ludwig Emile Antoine Maria (follows under VI) 
2 CONT 3. Maria Antonia Ludovica Blanka (0lgling, February 5, 1906 - May 4, 1908). 
2 CONT 4. Elisabeth Jeanne Antoinette Maria (0lgling, 1 June 1907 - +München, 2 February 1990) married on 11 June 1929 in Niederstotzingen Count Clemens Joseph Raymund Fugger van Kirchberg und zu Weisenhorn. 
2 CONT 5. Hedwige Henriette Française Antoinette (0lgling, 15 January 1909) married 25 July 1933 with Freiherr Max Ferdinand Karl van Venningen-Ullner van Diepurg.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''VI. LUDWIG EMILE ANTOINE VON MALDEGHEM''' (0lgling, 8 September 1904 - +16 November 1992) married Countess Ursula Saurma, Baroness van und zu der Teltsch (22 November 1904 - +4 December 1941).
2 CONT
2 CONT The systematic expulsion of Germans from eastern and southeastern Europe after the Second World War created a housing shortage everywhere. Under a Bodenreform, large landowners had to relinquish building land at fair prices. The b
2 CONC uilding in 1950-1951 of a new district in Niederstotzingen on Burgberger Strasse, of which the land belonged to Count Ludwig Emile, thus became possible. These grounds were already used by the population during the war to grow veg
2 CONC etables. Later the count sold land at the price of half a mark per square meter, a bargain price. This shows that the count, who led a previously withdrawn life, was nevertheless concerned with 'his' people. His funeral in 1992 wa
2 CONC s therefore impressive.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Ludwig Emile and Ursula are: 
2 CONT 1 . Karl Ludwig Maria Didier van Maldeghem, lives in Canada. 
2 CONT 2. Wolfgang and Angela van Maldeghem, Kühbach-Haslangkreit. 
2 CONT 3. Angela van Passavant, born of Maldeghem, Mannheim. 
2 CONT 4. Georg and Beate van Maldeghem, Schloss lgling bei Landsberg. 
2 CONT 5. Friedrich and Lilly van Maldeghem, Munich. 
2 CONT 6. Christine van Maffei, born of Maldeghem, Gut Hohenwettersbach.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Martens, Marc, translator. “MALDEGHEM DIE LOYALE.” De Heemkundige Kring Het Ambacht Maldegem, Jaarboek 6, 26 Dec. 2000, p. 42-50''
